fact-recursive.text:
Factorial: recursive
Explanation in simple steps
n! = n × (n−1)! with 0! = 1. Restrict input to 0..20 so results fit unsigned long long on conforming C implementations. Recursion uses a base case and decreasing argument; iteration accumulates a product.


Algorithm
Read n and reject values outside 0..20.
Compute factorial using base n<2 ->1; otherwise n*factorial(n-1).
Print result.


C program
#include <stdio.h>
unsigned long long factorial(unsigned n)
{
    return n<2 ? 1ULL : n*factorial(n-1);
}

int main(void)
